null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Outlook it expresses"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"direction-neutral, expecting price to settle near the centre strike"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Opens with"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"a credit"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Best case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Net credit received, at the centre strike"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Worst case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Wing width minus net credit"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Breakeven"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Centre strike minus credit, and centre strike plus credit"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Exposures"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"delta neutral · gamma negative · theta positive · vega negative"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-card border px-[18px] py-4 transition-colors duration-panel ease-standard bg-card border-border shadow-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":["$undefined",["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold leading-tight","children":["Lesson",false]}],false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted [&_h1]:mb-2 [&_h1]:text-base [&_h1]:font-bold [&_h1]:text-text [&_h2]:mb-1.5 [&_h2]:mt-5 [&_h2]:text-[13px] [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-text [&_h3]:mb-1 [&_h3]:mt-4 [&_h3]:text-[12px] [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-text [&_p]:mb-2.5 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-text [&_ul]:mb-2.5 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ol]:mb-2.5 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-bg [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:py-0.5 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_code]:text-text [&_table]:mb-3 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-left [&_table]:text-[11.5px] [&_th]:border-b [&_th]:border-border [&_th]:pb-1 [&_th]:pr-3 [&_th]:font-semibold [&_th]:text-text [&_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-border [&_td]:py-1 [&_td]:pr-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_a]:text-teal hover:[&_a]:underline [&_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&_blockquote]:border-border2 [&_blockquote]:pl-3 [&_blockquote]:italic","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Iron Butterfly"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"Four legs, one expiry: a short straddle at the centre strike, with a long put\r\nbelow and a long call above. Equivalently, a bull put spread and a bear call\r\nspread sharing the same short strike."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"The structure"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"A long put below the centre"}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"A short put at the centre"}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"A short call at the centre"}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"A long call above the centre"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":"Net credit, and a larger one than an iron condor of the same wing width,\r\nbecause the short legs are at the money rather than out of it."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"What it is exposed to"}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Theta"}]," positive and large — two at-the-money short legs carry the most\r\nextrinsic value available to decay."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Gamma"}]," negative and sharply so near the centre, bounded by the wings."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Vega"}]," negative, bounded."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"Against the iron condor"}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":"Same four-leg shape, same defined risk, different distribution."}],"\n",["$","table","table-0",{"children":[["$","thead","thead-0",{"children":["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","th","th-0",{}],["$","th","th-1",{"children":"Iron butterfly"}],["$","th","th-2",{"children":"Iron condor"}]]}]}],["$","tbody","tbody-0",{"children":[["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Short strikes"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Together, at the money"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Apart, out of the money"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-1",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Credit"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Larger"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Smaller"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-2",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Profit zone"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Narrow, peaked at the centre"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Wide, flat between shorts"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-3",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Probability of max profit"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Low"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Higher"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-4",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Risk-reward"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Better"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Worse"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":"The butterfly pays more and wins less often; the condor pays less and wins more\r\noften. Neither dominates. The butterfly's profit is a peak rather than a\r\nplateau — it is realised in full only if the underlying settles at the centre\r\nstrike, and it decays away from there in both directions."}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":["Notably, the butterfly's ",["$","em","em-0",{"children":"breakevens"}]," are often wider than its narrow profit\r\npeak suggests, because the credit received is large. A position can be\r\nprofitable across a reasonable range while only achieving maximum profit at one\r\npoint."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"Indian market specifics"}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Expiry-day pinning."}]," Underlyings sometimes settle close to strikes with\r\nlarge open interest, an effect associated with market-maker hedging and with\r\nthe max-pain concept — which is contested and carries low confidence in this\r\nrepo's own ontology (",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"knowledge-base/options/max-pain.yaml"}],"). An iron butterfly\r\nplaced at a high-open-interest strike is a position whose best outcome depends\r\non an effect that is not reliably established. It is worth knowing that the\r\nassociation is debated rather than assumed."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Weekly NIFTY concentration."}]," With NIFTY the only NSE index carrying weeklies\r\nsince November 2024, expiry-day butterflies concentrate there. Centre-strike\r\ngamma on a Tuesday afternoon is extreme; the wings are what make the structure\r\nsurvivable, and their width is the only thing standing between the position and\r\na full-width loss."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-10",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Costs."}]," Four legs each way. Because a butterfly's wings are typically\r\nnarrower than a condor's, cost as a fraction of maximum profit is high, and on\r\nvery narrow butterflies it can exceed the theoretical edge entirely."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-11",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Margin."}]," Defined-risk treatment, well below a naked short straddle. The 2%\r\nexpiry-day extreme loss margin applies to both short legs."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-12",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Physical settlement."}]," On a stock butterfly, an at-the-money short leg\r\nfinishing marginally in the money is assigned, creating a full-contract-value\r\nobligation on E+2. With both short legs at the same strike, one of them is\r\nnearly always in the money by some amount at settlement."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"How it typically fails"}],"\n",["$","p","p-13",{"children":"The underlying drifts away from the centre and stays there. Unlike a condor,\r\nwhich tolerates drift within a wide band, the butterfly starts losing\r\nimmediately as the underlying leaves the centre strike. The second failure is\r\ncost: on a narrow butterfly, eight legs of brokerage and STT against a small\r\ncredit leave very little margin for the position to be right."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-5",{"children":"Related"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-1",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/iron-condor.md"}]," — wider shorts, flatter payoff"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/short-straddle.md"}]," — the same core without wings"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"foundations/payoff-diagrams.md"}]," — reading a peaked payoff"]}],"\n"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] leading-relaxed text-faint","children":["Educational material describing how a structure behaves. Not a recommendation, not a signal, and not personalised advice. Source: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"font-mono","children":"docs/learning/strategies/volatility/iron-butterfly.md"}]]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children","$4","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":